@startuml metadata_runtime_directory_mapping
title Metadata to CampusAgent Runtime Directory

' Source evidence:
' pi-mono packages/coding-agent/src/core/skills.ts: Skill, loadSkillFromFile, formatSkillsForPrompt
' pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/context/ContextFileLoader.java: loadSystemPrompt
' pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/session/AgentSession.java: loadSkills
' Observed behavior: pi and pi-mono-java discover Skill metadata from SKILL.md frontmatter.
' Java divergence: the target compiler materializes only one controlled Agent directory.
' Target design: the Managed loader reads .campusagent only; legacy code keeps .campusclaw.
' Target design: RuntimeSessionStore persists Session state in a shared database.
' Target design: Agent and Model IDs use resource prefixes plus 24 alphanumeric characters.
' Design reason: raw case-sensitive Agent IDs require a case-sensitive root and collision guard.
' Target design: compiled settings.json carries Agent identity, version, default model, and model allowlist.
' Design reason: keep Agent-specific disclosure local while Managers remain runtime authorities.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #475569
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor #EFF6FF
  BorderColor #2563EB
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam file {
  BackgroundColor #F0FDF4
  BorderColor #16A34A
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam ArrowColor #475569

rectangle "Resolved metadata input" as Input {
  rectangle "AGENT\nid, version, system_prompt\nbinding_models, bindings, policy" as AgentMetadata
  rectangle "SKILL\nname, description, content\nskill and tool bindings" as SkillMetadata
  rectangle "TOOL\nid, name, description\nschema, source, permission" as ToolMetadata
}

rectangle "Runtime bundle compiler" as Compiler {
  rectangle "Validate versions, IDs,\ndependency closure,\ncase-fold conflicts and policy" as Validate
  rectangle "Render prompt and\nSkill resources" as Render
  rectangle "Publish Agent directory\natomically" as Publish
}

rectangle "Controlled Agent directory\ncase-sensitive file system\n<agent-runtime-root>/<agent-id>/" as AgentDirectory {
  file ".campusagent/settings.json\nagentId, agentVersion\ndefaultModel, enabledModels" as SettingsFile
  file ".campusagent/SYSTEM.md\nAgent instructions\nDirect Agent tool summaries" as SystemFile
  file ".campusagent/skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md\nFrontmatter and Skill content" as SkillFile
  file ".campusagent/skills/<skill-name>/references/tools.json\nDirect Skill tool summaries" as SkillToolsFile
}

database "Agent metadata authority\nAgent model and binding policy" as AgentAuthority
database "Tool Manager authority\nTool schema, status,\npermission and execution" as ToolManager
database "Model Manager authority\nModel descriptor,\nallowlist and invocation" as ModelManager
database "RuntimeSessionStore\nSession, Message, RunRecord,\nhistory sequence and revisions" as SessionStore

AgentMetadata --> Validate
SkillMetadata --> Validate
ToolMetadata --> Validate
Validate --> Render
Render --> Publish
Publish --> SettingsFile : identity, version and binding_models
Publish --> SystemFile : system_prompt and direct tools
Publish --> SkillFile : name, description and content
Publish --> SkillToolsFile : direct Skill tools

AgentMetadata ..> AgentAuthority : publish metadata
ToolMetadata ..> ToolManager : publish executable definition
SettingsFile ..> ModelManager : model selection snapshot
AgentMetadata ..> ModelManager : authoritative model bindings
AgentDirectory ..> SessionStore : pinned bundle revision

note right of SkillToolsFile
Only tool_id, name and description.
Schemas stay in Tool Manager.
Child Skill tools are not merged.
end note

note left of AgentDirectory
agent_id = agent_ + 24 alphanumeric characters
model_id = model_ + 24 alphanumeric characters
Compare IDs byte-for-byte.
Reject Agent ID case-fold collisions.
Verify directory and settings.json identity.
end note

note right of SettingsFile
defaultModel is binding_models[0].
enabledModels is a non-empty explicit allowlist.
Model Manager still revalidates every selection and invocation.
end note
@enduml

@startuml mate_agent_service_responsibility_boundary
title Public Chat and Runtime Service Responsibilities

' pi-mono-java baseline: 1f7a5423219edfa4519d8719f1cc8a188ed72873
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/ServerMode.java:260-285 run(), 377-391 wireServerRoutes()
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/ChatWebSocketHandler.java:115-135 handle(), 168-188 buildCloseHook()
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/SessionPool.java:186-202 getOrCreate(), 324-378 persistence
' Observed behavior: Java v1 routes /api/ws/chat directly to a handler and resolves one conversation-backed AgentSession.
' Target-only design: the mate-service public WebSocket, chat_id/session_id split, and internal WebSocket bridge do not exist in the baseline.
' Architecture change: mate-service owns public Chat orchestration; agent-service owns Runtime Session execution.
' Product constraint: the UI receives chat_id only; session_id remains an internal Runtime identifier.
' Design reason: separate user-facing Chat lifecycle from durable Agent Runtime identity and execution.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 18
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontColor #0F172A
skinparam ArrowColor #64748B
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #94A3B8
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam database {
  BorderColor #94A3B8
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  FontColor #334155
}

left to right direction

rectangle "Agent UI\n\nOpen public WebSocket\nSend agent_id, model_id, idempotency_key\nKeep chat_id\nRender public Chat Frames\nNever receive session_id" as UI #EFF6FF

rectangle "mate-service\n\nOwn public WebSocket and user authentication\nValidate protocol and connect idempotency\nEnforce fewer than 50 active Chats\nValidate product Agent and Model availability\nGenerate chat_id and session_id\nPersist Chat mapping and status\nRun guardrail, intent, and chain state\nOwn the internal Runtime WebSocket client\nRebuild public and internal Frames" as Mate #FFF7ED

rectangle "agent-service\n\nOwn internal Runtime WebSocket\nAuthenticate the calling service\nAuthoritatively validate Agent and Model\nCreate or restore Runtime Session\nBind Agent, Model, and bundle revision\nBuild Context and execute Model and Tools\nOwn Run, Message, and Runtime history" as Agent #ECFDF5

database "Mate Chat Store\n\nchat_id -> session_id\nChat state\nAgent and Model selection\nconnect idempotency result" as MateStore

database "RuntimeSessionStore\n\nSession state\nMessage and Run history\nAgent, Model, and bundle revision" as RuntimeStore

UI <--> Mate : Public WebSocket\nchat_id scope\npublic connection, request id, and seq
Mate <--> Agent : Internal WebSocket\nsession_id scope\nindependent connection, request id, and seq
Mate --> MateStore : Own and update
Agent --> RuntimeStore : Own and update

note bottom of Mate
The bridge is semantic, not byte-transparent.
HTTP 101, connection_id, generation, request id,
event seq, Ping/Pong, flow control, and close are hop-local.
This URL is an Agent Channel: only Runtime-routed sends
are accepted; other product channels use other contracts.
end note

note bottom of Agent
Runtime never reads chat_id, tenant_id, or user_id.
It uses session_id as the only Session key.
end note
@enduml

@startuml managed_session_context_assembly
title agent-service Internal Session and Context Assembly

' Source evidence:
' pi-mono packages/ai/src/types.ts: Context
' pi-mono packages/coding-agent/src/core/system-prompt.ts: buildSystemPrompt
' pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/session/AgentSession.java: initialize
' pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/SessionPool.java: getOrCreate
' pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/ServerMode.java: websocket route
' pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/ChatWebSocketHandler.java: handle
' pi-mono-java modules/agent-core/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/agent/loop/AgentLoop.java: invokeModel, toLlmTools
' Observed behavior: Java currently reads conversation_id during Upgrade and uses one base cwd.
' Observed behavior: AgentSession.initialize resolves a model before it creates the Agent.
' Java divergence: v2 authenticates Upgrade and maps closed Frames to a server-side SessionTransport.
' Architecture change: ManagedSessionTransport owns logical connection state; WebSocket is an adapter.
' Target design: globally unique session_id is the only SessionPool key; tenant and user stay upstream.
' Target design: a wss URI starts establishment; HTTP 101 establishes WebSocket transport.
' Target design: HTTP Upgrade and the first connect RequestFrame are separate protocol phases.
' Target design: mate-service is the internal Runtime client and supplies trusted session-affinity metadata.
' Target design: one Pod owns one active connection generation per Session.
' Target design: database history is authoritative; no target Session JSONL is generated.
' Target design: Managed settings is a compiled per-Agent file that does not exist in the Java baseline.
' Design reason: isolate prompt, model, tool, persistence, and run recovery across Agents.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam participant {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #475569
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam sequence {
  LifeLineBorderColor #64748B
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
  GroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
}

actor "mate-service\nRuntime bridge" as Client
participant "Trusted internal Gateway" as Auth
participant "ChatWebSocketAdapter" as WS
participant "SessionTransportFactory" as TransportFactory
participant "ManagedSessionTransport" as Transport
participant "AgentDirectoryResolver" as Resolver
participant "ManagedSettingsLoader" as SettingsLoader
participant "ManagedSessionPool" as Pool
participant "ManagedAgentSessionFactory" as Factory
participant "Model Manager" as ModelManager
participant "AgentSession" as Session
participant "AgentLoop" as Loop
participant "ManagedRunHub" as Hub
database "RuntimeSessionStore\nshared database" as Store

Client -> Client : call WebSocket library\nconnect(wss URI)
Client -> Auth : open one TCP connection\nthen TLS\nthen HTTP/1.1 GET\n/agent-service/internal/v1/ws/chat\nwith Upgrade and service auth context
Auth -> Auth : validate existing private-key or JWT auth\napply trusted Session affinity\nand validate Upgrade
Auth --> Client : HTTP/1.1 101 Switching Protocols
Auth --> WS : immutable connection auth context
WS -> TransportFactory : open(auth context)
TransportFactory --> WS : per-connection transport
Client -> WS : WebSocket Text Frame\nRequestFrame connect\nmode, session_id, agent_id, model_id?
WS -> WS : validate closed Frame
WS -> Transport : connect(command, invocation metadata)
Transport -> Resolver : resolve(agent_id)
Resolver -> Resolver : normalize and verify controlled root
Resolver --> Transport : agentCwd
Transport -> SettingsLoader : load(agentCwd/.campusagent/settings.json)
SettingsLoader -> SettingsLoader : verify agentId and agentVersion\nrequire non-empty unique enabledModels\nrequire defaultModel in enabledModels
SettingsLoader --> Transport : agentVersion, defaultModel, enabledModels
Transport -> Pool : open(session_id, agent_id)

alt mode=create
  Pool -> Pool : select requested model_id if supplied\notherwise settings.defaultModel
  Pool -> ModelManager : resolveModel(agent_id, effective model_id)
  ModelManager --> Pool : ModelDescriptor
else mode=resume
  Pool -> Store : load(session_id)
  Store --> Pool : Session, messages, revisions,\nand saved model_id
  Pool -> ModelManager : resolveModel(agent_id, effective model_id)
  ModelManager --> Pool : current ModelDescriptor
end

Pool -> Factory : create(session_id, agent_id, agentVersion,\nagentCwd, descriptor, restored messages)
Factory -> Factory : load controlled .campusagent\nSYSTEM.md and Skills
Factory -> Factory : register read, get_tool_info, call_tool
Factory -> Session : initialize isolated Session
Session -> Loop : systemPrompt, messages, AgentTools
Loop -> Loop : map AgentTools to Context.tools
Loop --> Pool : ready
Pool -> Hub : get active run for session_id
Transport -> Pool : increment connection generation\nand replace the old connection
Transport -> Hub : atomically register logical subscription\nand capture same-Pod cursor plus snapshot
Hub --> Transport : active_run snapshot and buffered publisher
Transport --> WS : SessionConnectResult
WS --> Client : ResponseFrame payload with session_id,\nconnection_generation, model, limits,\nfeatures and active_run
WS -> Transport : subscribe to events() after response write
Hub --> Transport : SessionEvents after snapshot cursor
Transport --> WS : ordered typed events
WS --> Client : EventFrames with connection seq

note over Factory,Loop
Managed prompt inputs:
Agent SYSTEM, three generic tools,
native Skill summaries, and cwd only.
end note

note over SettingsLoader,ModelManager
The HTTP create request supplies agent_id only.
The directory chooses the default candidate.
Model Manager remains the final authority.
end note

note over Pool,Store
Isolation key:
globally unique session_id
agent_id is an immutable binding.
Tenant and user belong upstream.
Pool retains AgentSession and the active-run reference; transport only subscribes.
AgentSession and AgentLoop execute; Hub maintains recovery state.
User-IP affinity is not a distributed owner.
Pod restart rebuilds from the database and marks the old run interrupted.
end note
@enduml

