' modules/ai/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/ai/types/ImageContent.java, lines 9-18
' docs/plans/ws-chat-followups.md, lines 12-37
' Observed behavior: both baselines can carry inline image content but do not
' define a generic attachment_id or an external Attachment Service.
' Target design: mate-service streams original bytes to shared OBS, records
' permanent identity state plus active lifecycle detail in shared openGauss,
' and exposes fixed HTTP upload, batch resolve, and content streaming APIs.
' Target design: the private OBS Object Key is exactly attachment_id; it is not
' an authorization token and never includes a prefix, path, or filename.
' Target design: deletion removes active detail and retains a five-field
' permanent DELETED tombstone in the t_attachment main table.
' Design reason: keep large-object transfer off the Chat control plane, support
' cross-Pod reads without local files, prevent metadata forgery, and retain
' reproducible public metadata snapshots in Runtime history.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #334155
  LifeLineBorderColor #64748B
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  ParticipantBorderColor #475569
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
  GroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
}

actor "End user" as User
participant "CampusMate client" as Client
participant "mate-service\nAttachment Service" as Attach
participant "background worker" as Worker
database "openGauss\nt_attachment\nt_attachment_active_detail" as DB
database "private OBS\nObject Key = attachment_id" as OBS
participant "mate-service\nRuntime client" as Upstream
participant "ChatWebSocketAdapter" as WS
participant "ManagedSessionTransport" as Transport
database "RuntimeSessionStore" as Store
participant "AttachmentInputAssembler" as Assembler
participant "Model Manager Provider" as Model

User -> Client : select one file
Client -> Attach : POST /mate-service/v1/chats/{chat_id}/attachments\nmultipart file + X-Attachment-Size\nPrefer respond-async or wait=N
Attach -> Attach : authorize user and session;\nrequire size 1..20 MiB and safe filename
Attach -> Attach : generate opaque attachment_id
Attach -> DB : INSERT t_attachment row\nand t_attachment_active_detail\nin one transaction
DB --> Attach : committed
Attach -> OBS : put(attachment_id, bounded stream,\nexpected_size_bytes) with create-only semantics
Attach -> Attach : count bytes, verify file-part EOF,\nand compute SHA-256 with backpressure

alt upload failed or actual size mismatch
  Attach -> OBS : delete(attachment_id) if an object may exist
  Attach -> DB : mark main FAILED;\nset bounded error_code in active detail
  Attach --> Client : bounded HTTP error
else OBS write succeeded
  OBS --> Attach : stored object completion
  Attach -> DB : update main PROCESSING;\nset size_bytes and SHA-256 in active detail
  Attach --> Client : 202 + Location + Retry-After\nunless wait reaches READY
  Worker -> DB : claim short scan lease in active detail\nusing retry time, lease, and row version
  Worker -> OBS : open(attachment_id) as stream
  OBS --> Worker : bounded byte stream
  Worker -> Worker : verify size and digest;\nsniff MIME and scan security;\nnever execute JavaScript
  Worker -> DB : mark main READY, BLOCKED, or FAILED;\nset detected MIME or bounded error_code;\nclear phase lease fields
  Client -> Attach : GET /mate-service/v1/chats/{chat_id}/attachments/{attachment_id}
  Attach -> DB : read authorized main and active detail
  DB --> Attach : status and public metadata
  Attach --> Client : 200 attachment resource
end

User -> Client : send text, attachments, or both
Client -> Upstream : application chat request
Upstream -> WS : RequestFrame chat.send\nordered attachment_ids + idempotency_key
WS -> Transport : typed SessionRequest + auth context
Transport -> Store : lookup accepted idempotency result

alt accepted result exists with the same payload
  Store --> Transport : original run_id and user_message_id
  Transport --> WS : accepted result
  WS --> Upstream : ResponseFrame before causal events
else first attempt
  Transport -> Transport : acquire Session single-writer guard;\nreject a different active run
  Transport -> Attach : POST /mate-service/internal/v1/attachments:resolve\nservice token + session_id + ordered IDs
  Attach -> DB : short transaction: lock main and detail;\nrequire same session, READY,\nactive detail present, and not expired
  alt any attachment is invalid
    DB --> Attach : rollback all changes
    Attach --> Transport : one safe batch error
    Transport --> WS : failed ResponseFrame; no run
  else all attachments are valid
    Attach -> DB : atomically preserve first referenced_at\nand set expires_at=NULL\nusing row_version compare-and-set
    DB --> Attach : committed public snapshots
    Attach --> Transport : ordered id, filename, media type,\nsize, and SHA-256
    Transport -> Store : commit user Message snapshots,\nidempotency result, run,\nand active run state
    Store --> Transport : run_id and user_message_id
    Transport --> WS : accepted result
    WS --> Upstream : ResponseFrame before run events

    Transport -> Assembler : ordered public snapshots
    loop each attachment
      Assembler -> Attach : GET /mate-service/internal/v1/sessions/{session_id}/\nattachments/{attachment_id}/content\nwith expected SHA-256
      Attach -> DB : require main READY, same session,\nreferenced_at not null, and matching digest
      DB --> Attach : authorized active metadata
      Attach -> OBS : open(attachment_id)
      OBS --> Attach : original byte stream
      Attach --> Assembler : bounded proxy stream
      Assembler -> Assembler : verify length and SHA-256;\nconstruct provider-neutral input
    end
    Assembler -> Model : optional text plus ordered attachments
    Model --> Transport : model stream
  end
end

group Public deletion
  Client -> Attach : DELETE unreferenced attachment
  Attach -> DB : conditional update to DELETING
  alt attachment is already referenced
    DB --> Attach : conflict
    Attach --> Client : 409 ATTACHMENT_REFERENCED
  else OBJECT_KEY_CONFLICT quarantine
    DB --> Attach : retain FAILED active detail
    Attach --> Client : bounded 503; audited reconciliation required
  else deletion accepted
    DB --> Attach : DELETING
    Attach --> Client : 202
    Worker -> DB : claim deletion lease in active detail
    Worker -> OBS : delete(attachment_id) with retry;\nnot found is success
    Worker -> DB : transaction: delete active detail;\nmark main DELETED and set deleted_at
  end
end

group Session deletion
  Upstream -> Transport : stop or abort Runtime Session
  Upstream -> Attach : delete all attachments for session_id
  Attach -> DB : mark normal non-DELETED rows DELETING; exclude quarantine
  Worker -> OBS : delete each attachment_id with retry
  Worker -> DB : delete each active detail and retain\npermanent five-field DELETED tombstones
  Attach --> Upstream : storage cleanup remains pending if quarantine exists
end

note over Client,OBS
Clients never access OBS directly.
The private Object Key is exactly attachment_id.
It has no prefix, path, filename, or public URL.
Knowing the ID is not authorization.
Upload retries create a new attachment_id.
Create-only conflict keeps FAILED detail for audited reconciliation
and never overwrites or deletes an object of unproven ownership.
The file body exists only in OBS; openGauss stores metadata.
end note

note over Attach,DB
The permanent main row retains only attachment_id, session_id,
status, created_at, and deleted_at after deletion.
The active detail exists only before DELETED.
referenced_at not null means the Session has referenced the file.
Referenced rows clear expires_at and cannot be deleted alone.
If Runtime persistence later fails, conservative retention lasts
until Session deletion; there is no release protocol.
end note

note over DB,Worker
Active detail roles:
filename is display metadata only.
detected_media_type and expected/actual sizes enforce content policy.
SHA-256 protects upload, scan, proxy, and Runtime integrity.
referenced_at and expires_at govern one-way reference and 24-hour cleanup.
error_code records a bounded safe failure reason.
attempt_count, next_attempt_at, lease_owner, lease_until,
and row_version provide retry, crash recovery, and race protection.
end note

note over WS,Attach
The WebSocket carries only ordered attachment_ids.
agent-service has no OBS endpoint, credentials, or direct access.
Object Key equality does not widen its authorization.
end note

note over Store,Model
Runtime history stores exactly attachment_id, filename,
media_type, size_bytes, and SHA-256.
File bodies are untrusted user data.
end note
@enduml

